Package: ludworks
Version: ${VERSION}
Architecture: ${ARCH}
Maintainer: Ludworks Project <maintainers@ludworks.invalid>
Depends: adduser
Recommends: ffmpeg
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://ludworks.readthedocs.io
Description: self-hosted, security-first NAS multitool
 Ludworks is a single server program that turns a disk into a private cloud:
 a web file manager with resumable uploads, retro "virtual TV channels" for a
 video library (with M3U, XMLTV and HDHomeRun tuner output), a notes app, an
 end-to-end-encrypted password vault and a lightweight spreadsheet app, behind
 one web UI and a documented HTTP API.
 .
 This package installs a hardened systemd service that runs as the
 unprivileged "ludworks" system user, serves HTTPS on port 8443 with a
 self-signed certificate and keeps its data in /var/lib/ludworks. The
 one-time setup token for the first administrator is written to
 /var/lib/ludworks/setup-token.txt.
 .
 ffmpeg is optional; it enables video thumbnails, transcoding and live
 MPEG-TS channel streams.
